data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_part.done","sequence_number":105,"item_id":"rs_071de21380ff09e7016aca70074e348190b61dd7580b909c82","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"part":{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Exploring server rendering**\n\nI’m thinking about implementing simple server-rendered HTML forms that don't require JavaScript in the browser. It seems like APIs aren't necessary for this, so I can use POST requests for `/projects` and handle redirects with server responses. I'll need to test with a temporary external OS to avoid artifacts while using fetch with persistence. Also, I should ensure that my HTML names are properly encoded and create directories as needed. I’ll structure the routes to get project details and create new entries while limiting the payload."}}

